  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "24. Core Abilities",
    "ruleNumber": "24.02",
    "summary": "Count repeated copies of an ability once. Whoever rolls decides which copy governs the roll. Make a fresh choice for duplicate weapon abilities whenever the unit uses that weapon to attack. When the ability has to work across every model, use the smallest value among them, as with **[Scouts](vsdata:core-rule/scouts)**. Examples include distance (**[Scouts 6″](vsdata:core-rule/scouts)** or **[8″](vsdata:core-rule/scouts)**), extra hit count (**[[SUSTAINED HITS 1]](vsdata:core-rule/sustained-hits)** or **[[SUSTAINED HITS 2]](vsdata:core-rule/sustained-hits)**), and target-specific thresholds (**[[ANTI-VEHICLE 4+]](vsdata:core-rule/anti)** or **[[ANTI-INFANTRY 2+]](vsdata:core-rule/anti)**).",
